	 * The OpenRegister task events the signing bridge consumes, as FQN
	 * string literals on purpose. `::class` on an imported name is a
	 * compile-time string too, but a literal keeps that true even if
	 * someone later adds the import — and during our own register() the
	 * `OCA\OpenRegister\` prefix is not on the autoloader yet, so neither a
	 * `class_exists()` probe (always false here) nor an eager reference
	 * (aborts register()) is an option; `BootstrapOrderIndependenceTest`
	 * pins both rules. Registering for an event class that never comes to
	 * exist is harmless: the dispatcher keys listeners by name, and the
	 * name is simply never dispatched. Mapping per openregister#3302
	 * (flow-approval-consolidation, approval-events-migration.md):
	 * transitioned-to-enabled replaces the retired step-initiated signal,
	 * committed terminality replaces step-approved and step-rejected, and
	 * sequence completion replaces chain completion.
	 *
	 * @var array<int, string>
	 */";s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀namespace";s:18:"OCA\Filinq\AppInfo";s:56:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀uses";a:4:{s:29:"documentsigningrequestedevent";s:46:"OCA\Filinq\Event\DocumentSigningRequestedEvent";s:32:"documentsigningrequestedlistener";s:57:"OCA\Filinq\EventListener\DocumentSigningRequestedListener";s:19:"signingtasklistener";s:44:"OCA\Filinq\EventListener\SigningTaskListener";s:20:"iregistrationcontext";s:47:"OCP\AppFramework\Bootstrap\IRegistrationContext";}s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀constUses";a:0:{}}}i:1;O:50:"PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode":11:{s:56:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀name";s:8:"register";s:58:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀phpDoc";O:50:"PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode":4:{s:64:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀phpDocString";s:225:"/**
