a:1:{s:44:"../../../lib/Service/DomainFolderGateway.php";a:1:{i:0;O:53:"PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedInterfaceNode":4:{s:59:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedInterfaceNode␀name";s:38:"OCA\Filinq\Service\DomainFolderGateway";s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedInterfaceNode␀phpDoc";O:50:"PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode":4:{s:64:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀phpDocString";s:1317:"/**
 * Reads and writes which groups may reach a folder.
 *
 * 🔑 THIS IS A SEAM BECAUSE THE STORAGE IS THE PART THAT REFUSES, and refusing
 * is the behaviour REQ-CDF-02 cares most about. An external mount can decline a
 * permission change, and the reconciler has to report that rather than claim
 * success. Putting the storage behind one narrow interface is what lets the
 * refusal be exercised at all: a test can make `revoke()` throw, which is the
 * scenario the requirement names and which no amount of real-mount testing on a
 * build host would reach.
 *
 * 🔴 THE NEXTCLOUD-BACKED IMPLEMENTATION IS NOT IN THIS CHANGE, AND THAT IS
 * MEASURED RATHER THAN CHOSEN. `OCP\Share\IManager` does not exist in this
 * repository's test environment: `interface_exists()` returns false under
 * `tests/bootstrap-unit.php`, while `OCP\Files\IRootFolder` returns true. So an
 * adapter written here could be neither run nor tested, only typed, and a
 * caller-less adapter that nobody can execute is exactly the shape this lane
 * keeps finding. It is named as what waits instead.
 *
 * Every method MAY throw. The service treats a throw as a refusal with a reason
 * and reports it; it never treats one as success.
 *
 * @spec openspec/changes/case-documents-and-the-flat-list/specs/document-register/spec.md
 */";s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀namespace";s:18:"OCA\Filinq\Service";s:56:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀uses";a:0:{}s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀constUses";a:0:{}}s:62:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedInterfaceNode␀extends";a:0:{}s:65:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedInterfaceNode␀statements";a:3:{i:0;O:50:"PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode":11:{s:56:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀name";s:16:"groupsWithAccess";s:58:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀phpDoc";O:50:"PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode":4:{s:64:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀phpDocString";s:302:"/**
