	 * Assert the dossier exists before (re)generating its summary.
	 *
	 * ⚠️ The name of this method overstates what it does, and the docblock it
	 * replaces overstated it further ("a successful resolution means the
	 * operator is permitted"). It is an EXISTENCE check. See
	 * `DossierSummaryDataService::assertDossierReadable()` for the measured
	 * reason: OpenRegister's RBAC cascade resolves to "configured nowhere" for
	 * the `dossier` schema, which OpenRegister treats as open, so the refusal
	 * this method relies on cannot fire for an existing dossier.
	 *
	 * What remains true: the HTTP layer (`DossierController`) does call this
	 * before `renderDossierSummary`, and the render itself deliberately runs
	 * as a system operation with RBAC disabled — so this call is the ONLY
	 * pre-render check there is, which is exactly why its real strength
	 * matters. Tracked in ConductionNL/filinq#441.
	 *
	 * @param string $dossierId The OR dossier object UUID.
	 *
	 * @return void
	 *
	 * @throws \RuntimeException 403 when the dossier cannot be resolved at all.
	 */";s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀namespace";s:18:"OCA\Filinq\Service";s:56:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀uses";a:7:{s:11:"iappmanager";s:19:"OCP\App\IAppManager";s:4:"file";s:14:"OCP\Files\File";s:11:"irootfolder";s:21:"OCP\Files\IRootFolder";s:5:"il10n";s:9:"OCP\IL10N";s:12:"iusersession";s:16:"OCP\IUserSession";s:18:"containerinterface";s:32:"Psr\Container\ContainerInterface";s:15:"loggerinterface";s:23:"Psr\Log\LoggerInterface";}s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀constUses";a:0:{}}s:57:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀byRef";b:0;s:58:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀public";b:1;s:59:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀private";b:0;s:60:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀abstract";b:0;s:57:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀final";b:0;s:58:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀static";b:0;s:62:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀returnType";s:4:"void";s:62:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀parameters";a:1:{i:0;O:53:"PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode":8:{s:59:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀name";s:9:"dossierId";s:59:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀type";s:6:"string";s:60:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀byRef";b:0;s:63:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀variadic";b:0;s:65:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀hasDefault";b:0;s:65:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀attributes";a:0:{}s:61:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀phpDoc";N;s:60:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedParameterNode␀flags";i:0;}}s:62:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀attributes";a:0:{}}i:4;O:50:"PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode":11:{s:56:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀name";s:20:"renderDossierSummary";s:58:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedMethodNode␀phpDoc";O:50:"PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode":4:{s:64:"␀PHPStan\Dependency\ExportedNode\ExportedPhpDocNode␀phpDocString";s:951:"/**
	 * Render the per-dossier summary PDF for one dossier.
	 *
	 * Aggregates anonymisation data across every file under the dossier's
	 * folder. The resulting PDF is written to a deterministic location
	 * (per Wave 2's `anonymisation-output-folder-layout` when shipped:
	 * `<dossier-folder>/anonymised/grondslagen.pdf`; until then:
	 * `<dossier-folder>/grondslagen.pdf`).
	 *
	 * On success the method also updates the dossier object's
	 * `configuration.grondslagen.{fileId, lastGeneratedAt}` so the dossier
	 * UI can badge the summary's freshness.
	 *
	 * @param string $dossierUuid The OR UUID of the dossier object.
	 *
	 * @return File The generated summary PDF.
	 *
	 * @throws \RuntimeException When the dossier can't be loaded, the folder
	 *                           isn't accessible, or rendering fails.
